        "comments": "The assembly cbRhyConf1.2 is based on 50x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Order and orientation of scaffolds on Chromosome 2 between\n22.40-22.63Mb and\n42.98-43.50Mb, Chromosome 4 between\n0.95-1.32Mb, SUPER_6 between\n25.37-25.57Mb, and Chromosome 9 between\n22.79-23.18Mb is unsure.",
